  {
   "id": "africa",
   "text": "Our oldest known fossils come from Jebel Irhoud, in Morocco, and they are about three hundred thousand years old. From Africa, people slowly spread across the planet. They reached Lake Mungo, in Australia, by around forty-two thousand years ago. They painted the caves of Lascaux. And they reached Monte Verde, in Chile, more than fourteen thousand years ago.",
