  {
   "id": "rivals",
   "text": "Two superpowers now ruled at opposite ends of the known world: Rome and Han China. Each governed tens of millions of people. Their armies never met, and they knew very little about each other. But their goods did meet, carried along one of the greatest trade networks in history.",
