  },
  {
   "id": "silkroad",
   "text": "The Silk Road. Caravans left Chang'an, crossed the desert oasis of Dunhuang, climbed the mountains to Samarkand and reached Antioch, near the Mediterranean. From there, goods sailed on to Rome. Silk, spices, glass and horses changed hands many times. And ideas travelled too, as Buddhism spread from India into China, while paper, invented in China, slowly made its way west.",
