   "id": "middle",
   "text": "In four seventy-six AD, the last Western Roman emperor lost his throne. But in the East, Rome lived on from Constantinople for almost a thousand years. In Baghdad, scholars at the House of Wisdom translated Greek books and advanced mathematics. Charlemagne was crowned emperor in eight hundred and ruled from Aachen. And Tang dynasty Chang'an was one of the largest cities on Earth.",
