   "id": "mongols",
   "text": "Then, out of the steppe, came the Mongols. In twelve oh-six, Genghis Khan united the Mongol tribes. Within a few decades, his armies swept across Central Asia, Persia and the lands of the Rus. By twelve seventy-nine, his grandson Kublai Khan ruled all of China, and the Mongol Empire covered about twenty-four million square kilometres, the largest connected land empire in history.",
