  {
   "id": "plague",
   "text": "Busy trade routes carried goods, but they also carried disease. In thirteen forty-seven, the Black Death reached Messina, in Sicily, and spread across Europe, killing tens of millions of people. Slowly, Europe recovered. In Mainz, Gutenberg's printing press made books cheap and fast to produce. And in fourteen fifty-three, the Ottomans captured Constantinople, ending the Byzantine Empire.",
