  {
   "id": "voyages",
   "text": "Columbus first landed on an island he named San Salvador. Six years later, Vasco da Gama sailed from Lisbon, around Africa, to Calicut, in India. And in fifteen twenty-two, the ship Victoria returned to Seville, completing the first voyage around the world, begun by Magellan and finished by Elcano. Maize, potatoes, silver and spices crossed the seas, but so did diseases that devastated the native peoples of the Americas.",
