  {
   "id": "atlantic",
   "text": "This new Atlantic world came at a terrible human cost. Over more than three centuries, more than ten million Africans were forcibly carried across the ocean and enslaved in the Americas, one of the largest forced migrations in history. Their labour built plantations and fortunes, and their descendants shaped the cultures of the Americas.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "map",
    "chapter": "The Atlantic World",
